{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786209992,"nonce":"diRqmL4PaK9TZBfcjFQH/4wF7sY=","title":"**What is wrong.** oto reads `config.original` from `GET /api/v2/status` but","message":"parses only two keys: `global` and `receivers`\n(`internal/sources/client/alertmanager/amconfig.go:62-65`). The `route` tree is\nnever parsed at all, so `group_wait`, `group_interval` and `repeat_interval` —\nwhether set on the top-level route or overridden on a child route — are not read.\nThe UI compensates by asking the operator to do the inheritance by hand:\n`web/src/features/settings/TuningSection.tsx:533` says \"Read these out of the\nroute your oto receiver is attached to, parents included\", and :539 admits \"oto\ncannot read these… these four numbers are entered here and kept in this browser\nonly\", defaulting to Alertmanager's own defaults with an \"Assumed, not yours\"\nbanner.\n\n**Why it matters.** Every tuning verdict oto gives — `refire_grace`, the flap\nwindow and threshold, the storm burst window — is arithmetic over those four\nnumbers (`docs/setup/tuning.md`, `internal/identity/domain/settings.go:114-141`).\nA real Alertmanager sets `group_interval` per route, so the number for oto's own\nreceiver is usually not the global one. An operator who leaves the defaults gets\nconfident advice about a cluster that is not theirs, and settings that \"can never\nfire\" are flagged as fine — or working ones flagged as broken. oto is already\nfetching the config that answers this.\n\n**Where.** `internal/sources/client/alertmanager/amconfig.go`,\n`internal/sources/client/alertmanager/client.go:206`,\n`web/src/features/settings/TuningSection.tsx:525-548`, `docs/setup/tuning.md`.\n\n**Done when.** `parseConfig` walks the route tree with Alertmanager's inheritance\nrules, resolves the timings for the route(s) that reach oto's receiver, exposes\nthem on the source health/status payload, and the tuning screen shows the real\nvalues with their source instead of asking the operator to type them — falling\nback to the manual entry only when the config is unreadable, and saying so.","files":null}]}